  "id": "COMPOUND:1074 - PROTEIN:1574",
  "verbalization": "Hesperetin is shown to have a target relationship with the Interleukin-5 receptor subunit alpha through multiple pathways, all of which involve the Cytochrome P450 1A2 enzyme. This enzyme is a common target of hesperetin, and its interaction with various compounds, including 2,5-Dimethyl-1,6-heptadiene and (2R)-7,4'-Dihydroxy-5-Methoxy-8-Methylflavan, ultimately leads to the activation of the Interleukin-5 receptor subunit alpha. The consistent presence of hesperetin as a target of multiple compounds that, in turn, target the Interleukin-5 receptor subunit alpha suggests a potential mechanism involving metabolic activation or enzyme-mediated signaling. The high scores across all three paths indicate a strong, reliable relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a plausible pathway where hesperetin influences the metabolic processing of certain compounds, which then exert their biological effects on the Interleukin-5 receptor subunit alpha.",
